> on an Alpha Workstation (OSF1/ Dec 4.0), but don't
> know the exact command to do this.
> 
> I want to communicate to it using Hayes commands.
> 
> ("cu" doesn't work, "tip (or whatever it's called) "
> doesn't work, also)

I've used both cu and tip to talk to a Hayes-style modem.  You need to do
some initial setup for either command before they're probably going to work.
If you're root you can update /etc/remote and /etc/acucap (for use with tip),
otherwise you can set environment variables to point to your own personal
copies of those files.

Check the man pages for tip, acucap(4), and remote(4).  If you go through
that procedure and still can't get it working, post your acucap and remote
entries and I or someone else can probably help you fix them up.

Tim
