In article <8dmnrs$3ju$1@nnrp1.deja.com> Eric Headley <ericheadley@my-deja.com> writes:
>When I try to login to an Alpha box running Digital Unix 4.0D I get the
>message "No shell".  This occurs for anyone except root.  I also cannot
>su to anyone.  What is going on ?

That means that the shell listed in the /etc/passwd field
is not found on your machine. E.G.:

duane:XXXXXXXXXXXX:1103:10:Andrew Duane USG:/home/duane:/bin/tcsh

the shell is /bin/tcsh. If this file doesn't exist, or is not
executable, you get "No Shell".

