> Hi all,
> 
> what must i do, that my printer prints ascii text files that contains
> characters like " �, � , �, �"
> 

If you're using the DEC multinational character set, you will need a
printer that understands it.  Don't expect an HP laser jet to do this. 
A printer with "digital" on the outside probably will understand this.

Alternativley, look for the characters in a more widely available
character set (like one of the ISO sets), or in a font from the list of
fonts that your printer understands.  Then figure out how to generate
those cahracters or request that font from your system.

