shl@cc.gatech.edu (Susan Liebeskind) writes:

>We are in the planning stages for upgrading some of our supported 
>applications from TruUnix 4.0D (formerly Digital Unix 4.0D) to 
>Tru64Unix 5.0 and are trying to track down some information about
>the upgrade process. 

>The big question:

>Is this a binary compatible release?  Can my existing applications run
>on a 5.0 platform without relinking?  Or is a relink and/or recompile
>necessary?  

You should run into few V4.0D programs that fail on V5.0.  I can't
recall running into any except Elisp programs that don't like xemacs.

You will run into lots of V5.0 problems that will fail when run on
V4.0D, so if backward compatibility is important, build on V4.0D.

(The problems are due to changing a few basic things like stat(2).  The
V4.0x code calls the old stat code, the V5.0 libraries call a new one
that returns more 64 bit data.)


