"man ftpd" tells you how to set it up. But I would say, if you want
anonymous ftp, don't use the vendor-supplied ftp server (on any brand of
unix). It's too easy for users on the system (or has been, that I've
seen) to change file permissions here and there so something will be
writable.

As you seem to be at an edu site, I've had good experience with ncftpd
(www.ncftpd.com), which is free to edu users. wu-ftpd seems to me to have
an unsettling frequency of security problems.

