We looked into the linker's sources at the assertion and
it looks like you might have a bad input object file.
Can you send me the object file that the linker is having
trouble with (uuencode or ftp address)?

Do the following to determine which object is being
processed at the time of the assertion failure.

If you're linking with the cc driver, then add "-Wl,-v" to
the command line.   If you're linking by calling ld
directly, then just add "-v" to the link line.
The verbose link will show you which object files the linker
is processing.  The one we're interested in is the one
that is opened just before the assertion failure.

