>machine  (some are already configured some are not)

The consvar(8) command will let you get and set console
variable, but I don't think that will help with what
you want.  Some systems include FRU message in the
error log when the system boots.  This might list some
of the devices found.  But, it may depend on the system
and operating system version, neither of which you've
provided.

If the kernel has been configured to recognize the devices,
but not setup ("configured" is a slightly overloaded word),
then they'll be listed in the boot messages.  For that you
need to know the device names that will be used, which
depends on the system and devices.  You might also try
"netstat -i", which will list interfaces.

