I can give you a few generic tests...

first, mountd needs to be running...if not, try the rc script that
fires it up.

also, do "rpcinfo -p" ....this should give you a list of rpc services
running on the host....nfs, mountd, portmapper, status and a couple of
other rpc.* services should be running.  Again, most of these, if not
active, should be fired up from an rc startup script.

This should be done on both machines - machine to be mounted and
machine that wants to mount.

