Many people post messages saying that a script works fine manually, but not
from cron.  This is almost always due to the fact that the script depends
on environment settings from their .profile, .login, or .cshrc.  Since none
of these are executed by a cron job, scripts that depend on them fail.

>I suspect that every time cron runs, restarts the 'dead' process, it then
>shuts down.  When cron shuts down, the processes are being killed.

I don't think so.

