In article <E472188161D5D311B08700105AF4CAAA0142D13F@kuumex03.barco.com> "fvda"
<filip.vandamme@barco.com> writes:

> In /dev I have device files for rz0* (internal HD) and rz4* (cdrom) only. If
> I add an extrenal hard disk, will reboot automatically create the appropriate
> device files in /dev or do I have to run a separate command on OSF1 V3.2?

No, the reboot will not create new device files for you.  However, you will be
able to create the device files quite simply, even before the reboot:  CD to
/dev and issue the command

	./MAKEDEV rzN

where N = the SCSI ID of the disk you will install.  (It may work better if you
do it after the reboot, but it's not *necessary*.)

Have fun!

