"fvda" <filip.vandamme@barco.com> writes:

>In /dev I have device files for rz0* (internal HD) and rz4* (cdrom) only. If
>I
>add an extrenal hard disk, will reboot automatically create the appropriate
>device files in /dev or do I have to run a separate command on OSF1 V3.2?

RMI covered the pre-V5.0 case.  In V5.0, things are _very_ different.
The disks are named /dev/disk/dsk0*, dsk1*, etc.  If you add a new disk
and reboot, the system will create /dev/disk/dsk<next>* for you.  The
main advantage to all this is you can add disks, move disks, take one
out for a while and put it back in later, and still use the same
device name.

I haven't figured out all the ins and outs myself yet.  The downside is
being able to point at a disk and know what it's device name must be
was handy.  (If you do "file /dev/rdisk/dsk13a" it will give you
controller/slot/LUN, so the information is still available.)

You won't have much trouble with it.

	-Ric Werme
